  "name": null,
  "problem": "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3}).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3})=$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "According to the sum and constant multiple rules, we can compute the required limit as follows:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3})=7{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)+8{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)-2{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe above equation assumes that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)$ both exist.\n\nIn part 5, we found that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=4,$ and from part 3, we found ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)=-1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3}) & =7{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)+8{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)-2{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 4+8\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =28-8-16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
